entityDescription:
University POLITEHNICA of Bucharest is the oldest and most prestigious engineer school in Romania. Its traditions are related to the establishment, in 1818, by Gheorghe Lazăr, of the first higher technical school with teaching in Romanian, at the Saint Sava Abbey in Bucharest. In 1832, it was reorganized into the St. Sava College. On 1 October 1864, The School of Bridges and Roads, Mines and Architecture was established, which becomes, on 30 October 1867, The School of Bridges, Roads and Mines, with a duration of 5 years. Under the leadership of Gheorghe Duca, on 1 April 1881, the institution acquires a new structure, under the name of The National School of Bridges and Roads; on 10 June 1920, the Politehnica School of Bucharest was founded, with four departments: Electromechanics, Civil Engineering, Mines and Metallurgy, Industrial Section. From November 1920 the name changes to POLITEHNICA of Bucharest. On 3 August 1948, the Polytechnic Institute of Bucharest was founded, which initially included 4 faculties and in which, since 1950, have appeared most of the current faculties. Based on the resolution of the Senate of November 1992, the Polytechnic Institute of Bucharest became University POLITEHNICA of Bucharest. (https://upb.ro/en/upb-history/)
The Research Center for Aeronautics and Space - CCAS was established in 2001 becoming a component of research activity in University POLITEHNICA of Bucharest, which enjoys a long and fruitful tradition. The philosophy of the CCAS is to maintain a balance between theoretical research and practical applications in projects involving aerospace technologies. With this aim, the objectives of CCAS activity include:
-Developing close links with major companies, SME, research institutes, and higher education units through specific research projects;
-Helping industry to exploit new advanced technologies in aerospace domain and improve human research potential;
-Stimulating and developing the cooperation in the fields of research initiatives in European Union.

Area of expertise: 

-Fluid mechanics, flow studies ¿ industrial systems and bioengineering; 
-Flow simulation and optimal aerodynamics modeling for air transport and space vehicles;
-Aerodynamic design of wind turbines with horizontal or vertical axis and wind propellers, performances;
-Modern systems of lubrication and applications in industry;
-Thermo-hydraulic systems, analysis and design;
-Fluid structure Interaction, aero-elastic phenomena; 
-Calculation and design of aircraft structures, composite structures; 
-Propulsion systems;
-Aircraft dynamics, flight control and simulation;
-Avionics, sensors and actuators;
-Air Traffic Management;
-Hybrid rocket motors;
-Small satellites, attitude control and structure analysis;
-Small launchers, sounding rockets, jet control systems;
-Civil rocket systems;
-Industrial Design and Computer Assisted Design; 
(http://www.upb-ccas.ro)

